WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.920
Smells are all around us.
气味无处不在。

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:09.940
What we know as a scent is a collection of natural or artificial airborne chemicals released from objects.
我们所说的气味，是从物体中释放出来的、飘散在空气中的天然或人造化学物质的集合。

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.210
But smell is often overlooked and undervalued.
但嗅觉常常被忽视，也被低估。

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:20.290
So, as climate change and biodiversity loss threaten natural scents, many people may not even notice.
因此，当气候变化和生物多样性丧失威胁到自然界的气味时，许多人甚至可能察觉不到。

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:26.410
Whether or not we pay attention to the world’s “scentscape”, heat and pollution are causing it to shift.
无论我们是否留意世界的“气味景观”，高温和污染都在使它发生变化。

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:37.170
As temperatures rise, man-made substances release more scent molecules, and biodiversity loss due to climate change threatens the plants that scent the environment.
随着气温升高，人造物质会释放更多的气味分子；而气候变化导致的生物多样性丧失，也威胁着那些为环境增添气味的植物。

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.840
“If you go to a forest, you have a given environment and temperature.
“如果你走进一片森林，那里有特定的环境和温度。

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:56.700
If that temperature goes a little bit higher, the profile of the chemical components in the air changes,” explains John Smith, a chemical engineer — temperature can affect the number of smell-carrying gas particles released from substances.
如果温度再升高一点，空气中化学成分的构成就会改变，”化学工程师约翰·史密斯解释说，这是因为温度会影响物质释放出的、携带气味的气体粒子的数量。

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.080
“And therefore, the perception of how the forest smells changes.”
“因此，人们对这片森林气味的感知也会改变。”

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.940
That effect extends beyond forests.
这种影响不仅限于森林。

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:13.720
Snow — already threatened by a warming climate — absorbs different chemicals from the atmosphere as temperatures rise, which changes its cold-clean scent.
雪本身已经受到气候变暖的威胁；随着气温升高，雪会从大气中吸收不同的化学物质，这会改变它那种清冷干净的气味。

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:21.490
Warmer conditions can intensify smells, leading the snow to smell more unpleasant and potentially gather more pollutants.
更温暖的环境会使气味变得更浓，让雪的气味更难闻，还可能让雪聚集更多的污染物。

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:28.330
Climate change is also quickening the loss of biodiversity, threatening to erase certain smells entirely.
气候变化还在加速生物多样性的丧失，可能会让某些气味彻底消失。

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:33.030
When plants disappear, their scents become more difficult to produce.
植物消失了，它们的气味也就更难产生了。

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:36.240
Some scents are linked to cultural heritage.
有些气味与文化遗产相关。

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:45.240
A recent study reported that native communities in Peru noticed a change in the smell of the Amazon River due to industrial pollution.
最近的一项研究报告称，秘鲁的原住民社区注意到，由于工业污染，亚马孙河的气味发生了变化。

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:54.210
Over generations, communities became desensitised to increasingly smelly rivers, a sign of broader ecosystem degradation.
一代又一代人下来，这些社区对越来越难闻的河流变得麻木了——河流越来越难闻，是生态系统更大范围退化的一个迹象。

00:01:55.010 --> 00:02:04.880
At the same time, in some Amazonian belief systems, declining water quality and the unpleasant smells will lead to the dispersal of the river’s spiritual beings.
与此同时，在亚马孙地区的一些信仰体系中，水质下降和难闻的气味会导致河中的神灵消散。

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.530
The damage to the scentscape could result in harm to both health and spiritual practice.
对气味景观的破坏，可能会同时危害人们的健康和精神信仰活动。

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:22.150
Even though we have other valuable things endangered by climate change, like food access, there is also an element of cultural identity, cultural survival, and history.
尽管还有其他宝贵的东西受到气候变化的威胁，比如获取食物的途径，但气味中也包含着文化认同、文化存续和历史的元素。

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.310
If we don’t look at it, we lose all the richness behind it.
如果我们不去关注它，就会失去它背后的全部丰富内涵。
